* t47break.a -- CONF68K test t47: SS_Break disconnects a pipe path.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): pipeman's SetStat list gives SS_Break as "Forces* disconnection", and the error-code appendix names a pipe among the three* ways a path is lost -- "A pipe path has been broken due to an SS_Break* SetStat" (E$PthLost, 000:173). Between them the two passages say what a* read after SS_Break must report, and that is what this test observes.** Nothing is written to the pipe, and that is deliberate: a read on a pipe* nobody is writing to reports E$EOF, which is exactly the answer this test* must NOT see. E$EOF says the writers finished; E$PthLost says the path was* taken away underneath the reader. A system that answers 211 here FAILs, and* that is the disagreement worth looking at.** A system with no SS_Break at all never reaches the read: it reports the* SetStat's own error instead (E$UnkSvc, 208), which FAILs too and says which* half is missing.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1IOpen set $84IRead set $89ISetStt set $8EIClose set $8FSSBreak set $001D*EXPECT set 173* psect t47break,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart* Scratch buffer on the stack, never in the code psect: this module is* marked re-entrant and a real system may hold it in ROM. sub.l #128,a7 movea.l a7,a4 lea pipename(pc),a0 moveq #3,d0 trap #0 dc.w IOpen bcs.w setuperr move.w d0,d7 moveq #0,d6* --- force the disconnection moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 move.w #SSBreak,d1 trap #0 dc.w ISetStt bcc.s broke move.w d1,d6 bra.s done* --- and read the path it disconnectedbroke moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 moveq #1,d1 movea.l a4,a0 trap #0 dc.w IRead bcc.s done move.w d1,d6done moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IClose cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.s ispass bra.s isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*pipename dc.b "/pipe",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t47 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  a read after SS_Break on a pipe reports E$PthLost",0 ends